mfr.lua -- an output formatter for Lua
======================================

mfr is a simple Lua module with functions for prettifying output, such
as setting the foreground colour of text in the terminal.

Building and installing
-----------------------

Download the module with LuaRocks:

    luarocks install mfr

Using it
--------

Import it with

    mfr = require("mfr")

and use any of the functions listed in docs/index.html, for example:

    mfr.describe_fg_colors()

Documentation
-------------

The function reference is in docs/index.html, generated with ldoc by
gendocs.sh.  It is also available on GitHub Pages:

    https://mb6ockatf.github.io/mfr.lua/

Unit tests
----------

The unit tests are written with busted
(https://github.com/lunarmodules/busted).  Run them with ./test.lua.
Please note that system-dependent tests are not run (if your terminal
does not support colours, the corresponding functionality is not
checked).  Output functions are not tested either.

Reporting bugs
--------------

This repository is open for contribution.  You are welcome to submit
ideas and bug reports at https://github.com/mb6ockatf/mfr.lua/issues.

